From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:09:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fit in the 4 MiB of the DS

The DS has 4 MiB of RAM in total, so the minimum memory is 2 MiB. It has
no network play, so there is one client slot instead of at least four,
512 particles instead of 2048, and with less than 8 MiB the server has
448 edicts instead of 600, still plenty for the id maps, ED_Alloc checks
that limit. The pack
directory, up to 128 KiB, is read into temporary hunk memory instead of
onto the stack.

The cache holds less than the models of a level, which made it push out
what was in use:

- The hunk growing into the cache threw out the data in its way, often a
  model drawn every frame. That data now moves away, what was used the
  longest ago goes instead when there is no room.
- An alias model took three times its size while it loaded: the file,
  the model built from it and its copy in the cache. The file is freed
  before the copy, else the model pushed out another one drawn every
  frame, which pushed it out again, e1m3 ran at 2 fps.
- A driver that loads the sounds that play every frame can let them wait
  (S_LoadSoundUnused), they and the files they are read from only push
  out data that wasn't used in the last 10 frames (Cache_AllocUnused,
  Cache_RoomUnused). A driver that plays straight from
  the cache is told when data is freed or moved (cache_freehook).
- The server and client asked for the models of a level one after the
  other, reading each again as it had been pushed out by the others. For
  them only the header of an alias model is read (Mod_LoadAliasHeader),
  what they use is in its model_t, its frames are read when it's drawn.
  A level loads up to 40% faster.
